__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info
.venv
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
credentials.json
node_modules/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.langgraph_api/
.DS_Store

# Per-developer Claude Code state (settings.local.json is machine-specific permissions).
# The tracked CLAUDE.md files are the checked-in half and stay in git.
.claude/

# Node modules for the artifact components in ui/. The lockfile beside them IS tracked:
# langgraph.json bundles ui/ui.tsx at build time, so the bundle's dependencies need to
# resolve to the same versions everywhere.
ui/node_modules/

# The Node setup installs when the machine has none it can use (`install_node`), and the
# staging directory it unpacks into first.
/.node/
/.node.partial/

# The chat frontend `scripts/setup.py` clones. A checkout of someone else's repo,
# vendored here only so the UI needs no directory outside this one — also in
# .dockerignore, or a dev-only Next app ships inside the deploy image.
.chat-ui/

# Host-side cache. Not a deliverable, and `data/` is 20M+ of fetched abstracts that
# anyone can re-fetch.
data/

# Local scratch: design notes, API probe notes, eval planning and per-sweep reports. None
# of it is input to the agent or the eval harness — the canonical seeds are
# evals/datasets/*.yaml.
docs/
AUDIT.md
evals/datasets/archive/
evals/taxonomy/
evals/ground_truth_reports/
evals/failure_reports/
evals/proposals/
evals/references/
evals/reports/
scripts/eval_misses.py
sniff_deprecated.py

# Example attachments for trying the composer by hand: one file per UPLOAD_KINDS kind.
# 3 MB of PDFs, figures and reference exports that nothing at run time reads — also in
# .dockerignore. Kept on disk, out of the repo: samples/README.md, itself untracked,
# records where each one came from.
samples/

# Scratch corpus: READMEs of ~100 comparable open-source vertical agents, pulled for
# a one-off comparison of our README against theirs. Nothing reads it at run time.
readme_research/

# Local logo explorations and preview exports.
/logo-concepts/

# Cache and saved answers for the `engine-demo` branches' `scripts/engine_demo.py`, which
# points `DEEP_LIFE_SCI_DATA_DIR` here. Kept out of `data/` on purpose: those runs carry a
# planted bug, so their cache must not be the one the healthy agent reads. Ignored on main
# too because the directory survives a branch switch.
data-engine-demo/
